#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133576 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133767 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e023193-7494-5e3a-bd6e-e15ae0e9a1bd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Norm of a Vector in an Inner Product Space of Polynomials"}] :question/id #uuid "105a5a4a-2fea-54bb-97c6-c2a700b05f61" :question/math-academy-id "e-5548" :question/problem "Let $V=\\mathbb{R}_2[t]$ be the vector space of all polynomials of degree at most $2,$ equipped with the inner product\n\n$$\n\\langle {x}(t), {y}(t) \\rangle = x(1)y(1) + x(2)y(2) + x(3)y(3).\n$$\n\nCalculate the norm of the vector  $p(t) = 1 - t^2.$" :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $p(t)$ with respect to an inner product $\\langle \\cdot, \\cdot \\rangle$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖p(t)‖=\\sqrt{⟨p(t),p(t)⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${p}(t) = 1-t^2,$ we obtain\n\n$$\np(1)=0,\\qquad \np(2)= -3,\\qquad \np(3)=-8.\n$$\n\nComputing $\\|p(t)\\|$ using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖p(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{⟨p(t),p(t)⟩} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{p(1)p(1)+p(2)p(2)+p(3)p(3)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{[p(1)]^{2}+[p(2)]^{2}+[p(3)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(0)^{2}+(-3)^{2}+(-8)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0+9+64} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{73}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133577 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133768 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "090d6747-55e2-548b-84f2-88f6c732518f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Norm of a Vector in an Inner Product Space of Continuous Functions"}] :question/id #uuid "5aafdd7d-939a-5690-ac4d-46b554524d75" :question/math-academy-id "e-5549" :question/problem "Let $V=\\mathcal{C}\\left[0,1\\right]$ be the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $\\left[0,1\\right],$ equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n\\langle x(t),y(t) \\rangle = \\displaystyle\\int_{0}^{1} x(t) y(t) \\, \\textrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nCalculate the norm of the vector $f(t)= 2t-1.$" :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $f(t)$ with respect to an inner product $\\langle \\cdot, \\cdot \\rangle$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\| f(t)\\| = \\sqrt{\\langle  f(t),  f(t) \\rangle}.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(t),f(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(f(t))^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(2t-1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(4{t}^{2}-4t+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={(\\frac{4{t}^{3}}{3}-2{t}^{2}+t)|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}-2+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\| f(t)\\| = \\sqrt{\\dfrac{1}{3}} = \\dfrac{\\sqrt 3}{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133578 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133769 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "466fb505-1ff3-5b27-a5f7-0ea5b31b2927" :knowledge-point/title "Normalizing a Vector in an Inner Product Space"}] :question/id #uuid "d279bb1d-754e-5044-9a01-d4c86f30b269" :question/math-academy-id "e-5550" :question/problem "Let $V=\\mathcal{C}\\left[0,\\pi\\right]$ be the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $\\left[0,\\pi\\right],$ equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n\\langle x(t),y(t) \\rangle = \\displaystyle\\int_{0}^{\\pi} x(t) y(t) \\, \\textrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nNormalize the vector $f(t)= 3t.$" :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $f(t)$ with respect to an inner product $\\langle \\cdot, \\cdot \\rangle$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\| f(t)\\| = \\sqrt{\\langle  f(t),  f(t) \\rangle}.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(t),f(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{(3t)}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }9{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =3{t}^{3}\\,{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =3{\\pi }^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\| f(t) \\|  = \\sqrt{3\\pi^3} = \\pi \\sqrt{3\\pi}.\n$$\n\nTo normalize the vector $f(t),$ we divide $f(t)$ by its norm $\\| f(t) \\| \\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t) & =\\frac{f(t)}{‖f(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi \\sqrt{3\\pi }}\\cdot 3t \\\\  & =\\frac{t\\sqrt{3}}{\\pi \\sqrt{\\pi }}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133629 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133814 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "92053541-63fa-5cca-b3d8-0f4864c31051" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Norm of a Vector With Respect to a Given Inner Product"}] :question/id #uuid "35e7ce1a-b2cc-50dd-8bf7-24d20e55d623" :question/math-academy-id "e-5908" :question/problem "An inner product on $V = \\mathbb{R}^3$ is defined as $\\langle \\mathbf{x}, \\mathbf{y} \\rangle =  2x_1 y_1 + x_2 y_2 + 3x_3 y_3.$ \nCalculate the norm of the vector ![](images/59/596d25646a513272f62708b9370136c1ef45a120edee3a4454c1a559119be3e5.svg) under this inner product." :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $\\mathbf v$ with respect to an inner product $\\langle \\cdot, \\cdot \\rangle$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖=\\sqrt{⟨v,v⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $\\|\\mathbf{v}\\|$ using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖ & =\\sqrt{⟨v,v⟩} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2\\cdot (3\\cdot 3)+2\\cdot 2+3\\cdot (1\\cdot 1)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{18+4+3} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529087 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133814 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "92053541-63fa-5cca-b3d8-0f4864c31051" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Norm of a Vector With Respect to a Given Inner Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20e15b4c-4991-5dc9-8b45-ed10cc092a7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528390} {:answer/id #uuid "4a53b2d0-48eb-5228-9ea2-2000e2948d59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528485} {:answer/id #uuid "5aae46bc-e0c9-5b85-8008-b239c57b2c11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528514} {:answer/id #uuid "d1ffc7c4-55dc-5d3f-b3b3-8c34240ac735" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528821} {:answer/id #uuid "f3b898d0-2a91-50f3-ba29-21df42a1673f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528900}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20e15b4c-4991-5dc9-8b45-ed10cc092a7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528390} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3a6e30f-e49a-55e3-89a2-979eca32e275" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529057}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "01f92ee9-73cd-5c08-adfa-addc2317087e" :question/math-academy-id "q-141165" :question/problem "An inner product on $V={R}^{3}$ is defined as $⟨x,y⟩=3{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+5{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+{x}_{3}{y}_{3}.$ \nCalculate the norm of the vector $v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ under this inner product." :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $v$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖=\\sqrt{⟨v,v⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $‖v‖$ using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖ & =\\sqrt{⟨v,v⟩} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3\\cdot (1\\cdot 1)+5\\cdot ((-1)\\cdot (-2))+2\\cdot 2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3+5+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{12} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272230 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133767 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e023193-7494-5e3a-bd6e-e15ae0e9a1bd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Norm of a Vector in an Inner Product Space of Polynomials"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ed52fa3-c50c-531a-84bd-93ca5acb551d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270378} {:answer/id #uuid "a72c37fd-0620-58d9-8f2e-b9ce2d3f324d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270764} {:answer/id #uuid "b982e71c-07f8-5618-8bc3-c261a6e66b10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{21}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270907} {:answer/id #uuid "e4fd85c2-cdb0-554f-890c-9bf153e09b24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271288} {:answer/id #uuid "eb408961-8bee-545a-9bb6-00c8d51979e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{21}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271332}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b982e71c-07f8-5618-8bc3-c261a6e66b10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{21}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270907} :answer-field/id #uuid "dcd08076-d47b-5b25-8a84-1723a58999f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271897}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5af30cbe-62d3-5504-84b8-034b67c250b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-141167" :question/problem "Let $V={R}_{2}[t]$ be the vector space of all polynomials of degree at most $2,$ equipped with the inner product\n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩=x(1)y(1)+x(2)y(2)+x(3)y(3).\n$$\n\nCalculate the norm of the vector $p(t)=2-t+{t}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $p(t)$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖p(t)‖=\\sqrt{⟨p(t),p(t)⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $p(t)=2-t+{t}^{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\np(1)=2,\\,p(2)=4,\\,p(3)=8.\n$$\n\nComputing $‖p(t)‖$ using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖p(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{⟨p(t),p(t)⟩} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{p(1)p(1)+p(2)p(2)+p(3)p(3)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{[p(1)]^{2}+[p(2)]^{2}+[p(3)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}+{8}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+16+64} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{84} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{21}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272232 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133768 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "090d6747-55e2-548b-84f2-88f6c732518f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Norm of a Vector in an Inner Product Space of Continuous Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "137334f5-2538-5bbe-adf3-1c3ee6f82723" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269441} {:answer/id #uuid "4f3ce5f7-b475-590c-85ef-81d3c59b439d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269983} {:answer/id #uuid "5487d164-9c18-5464-89ce-e01d5d908063" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270023} {:answer/id #uuid "a55acb1e-c700-5253-ad95-6dcec8339623" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270749} {:answer/id #uuid "f5c1cc2f-b46c-57f6-b3bd-a5c653af9573" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271426}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5487d164-9c18-5464-89ce-e01d5d908063" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270023} :answer-field/id #uuid "e46c7c52-6bda-5582-87b7-a69e90624253" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271914}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4c4a016c-b4a0-506e-993b-378d9e3fc8f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-141170" :question/problem "Let $V=C[-1,1]$ be the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[-1,1],$ equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{-1}^{1}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nCalculate the norm of the vector $f(t)=1-t.$" :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $f(t)$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n‖f(t)‖=\\sqrt{⟨f(t),f(t)⟩}.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(t),f(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}(f(t))^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}(1-t)^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}({t}^{2}-2t+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}-{t}^{2}+t)|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{3}-1+1)-(\\frac{(-1)^{3}}{3}-(-1)^{2}+(-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n‖f(t)‖=\\sqrt{\\frac{8}{3}}=2\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272234 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133769 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "466fb505-1ff3-5b27-a5f7-0ea5b31b2927" :knowledge-point/title "Normalizing a Vector in an Inner Product Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c9ae6fc-9aa9-57c9-aa7c-b9b35d5c3ad5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269378} {:answer/id #uuid "45e1e67b-c416-5d88-b08f-b940b6be61c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269908} {:answer/id #uuid "75a81aa3-52ba-5a54-9fa3-867b63ae2c07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{6}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270307} {:answer/id #uuid "987711fa-325e-55b8-ae43-bbd30245c57f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270612} {:answer/id #uuid "ebe2dd75-e051-5fc3-a230-fc57a3dc2eb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271342}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "987711fa-325e-55b8-ae43-bbd30245c57f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270612} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5513a7d-da83-50ea-881c-42cda4359bb3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271809}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "afb4bbee-f88e-55e1-b82e-818f2d9c1c71" :question/math-academy-id "q-141174" :question/problem "An inner product on $V={R}^{3}$ is defined as $⟨x,y⟩={x}_{1}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+{x}_{3}{y}_{3}.$ \n\nNormalize the  vector  $v=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$ under this inner product." :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $v$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖=\\sqrt{⟨v,v⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨v,v⟩ & =2\\cdot 2+3\\cdot 1\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =4+3+1 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖ & =\\sqrt{8}=2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo normalize the vector $v$, we divide $v$ by its norm $‖v‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{v}{‖v‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134402 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133768 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "090d6747-55e2-548b-84f2-88f6c732518f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Norm of a Vector in an Inner Product Space of Continuous Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19300905-4466-5aa7-b885-59a224072f16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385437} {:answer/id #uuid "4a5f44b2-7f86-5b68-b027-950c850a9847" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{10}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385438} {:answer/id #uuid "22e23866-42c6-5eec-9adb-06a6177fad2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385439} {:answer/id #uuid "469852f6-e362-57f2-b417-b281cb485bc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385440} {:answer/id #uuid "6a73f1bb-94fc-5ac7-b940-dd446230b9fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{19}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385441}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a73f1bb-94fc-5ac7-b940-dd446230b9fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{19}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385441} :answer-field/id #uuid "51f9f72a-e7b3-5c78-ba0f-fa72d34021ec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186385436}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8deaf7d6-385c-55e1-887e-dce5bcf25e8c" :question/math-academy-id "q-42727" :question/problem "Let $V=C[0,1]$ be the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[0,1],$ equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{1}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nCalculate the norm of the vector $f(t)=t+2.$" :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $f(t)$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n‖f(t)‖=\\sqrt{⟨f(t),f(t)⟩}.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(t),f(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(f(t))^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(t+2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({t}^{2}+4t+4)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}+2{t}^{2}+4t)|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}+2+4 \\\\  & =\\frac{19}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n‖f(t)‖=\\sqrt{\\frac{19}{3}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329682 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133769 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "466fb505-1ff3-5b27-a5f7-0ea5b31b2927" :knowledge-point/title "Normalizing a Vector in an Inner Product Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "165933c2-6b08-53c0-b905-d5ec59e56a60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4(t-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327129} {:answer/id #uuid "e27f066c-37c1-59a9-98d6-175e81fd7e34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328917} {:answer/id #uuid "f0aed3d2-6b41-5076-b071-462dc43554ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}(t-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329035} {:answer/id #uuid "f3298422-dd2e-5f10-8faa-ac2572ee58dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}(t-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329058} {:answer/id #uuid "f6aef26c-92d8-505d-bf2e-1e5a4b1adb2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}(t-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329098}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f3298422-dd2e-5f10-8faa-ac2572ee58dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}(t-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329058} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae5be7f0-c577-5334-886d-25eb95c97df6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329488}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1aca67bb-ce76-56b0-b16e-e131cb0a90bb" :question/math-academy-id "q-42739" :question/problem "Let $V=C[0,1]$ be the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[0,1],$ equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{1}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nNormalize the vector $f(t)=t-1.$" :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $f(t)$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n‖f(t)‖=\\sqrt{⟨f(t),f(t)⟩}.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(t),f(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{(t-1)}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,({t}^{2}-2t+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}-{t}^{2}+t)|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}-1+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n‖f(t)‖=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}.\n$$\n\nTo normalize the vector $f(t),$ we divide $f(t)$ by its norm $‖f(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t) & =\\frac{f(t)}{‖f(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{t-1}{(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}})} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}(t-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329684 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133768 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "090d6747-55e2-548b-84f2-88f6c732518f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Norm of a Vector in an Inner Product Space of Continuous Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1be49c51-c784-51a6-8de7-aa0d618894f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327177} {:answer/id #uuid "4ce47b80-c117-53ab-90db-09ba10715757" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327601} {:answer/id #uuid "57f15f87-5ac5-5105-a84b-1e669b010006" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{\\sqrt{15}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327705} {:answer/id #uuid "a884f908-d848-522d-91ba-08faeb45fa6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{256}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328393} {:answer/id #uuid "c1d8d0fc-c7d3-5bb3-8c43-495ac03e1a83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328626}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "57f15f87-5ac5-5105-a84b-1e669b010006" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{\\sqrt{15}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327705} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1a2cca8-b62c-5d45-9d46-64119bd74bc8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329603}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "375ba5e6-834f-57c0-93fa-8f94e8570128" :question/math-academy-id "q-42763" :question/problem "Let $V=C[0,2]$ be the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[0,2],$ equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{2}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nCalculate the norm of the vector $f(t)=t+{t}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $f(t)$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n‖f(t)‖=\\sqrt{⟨f(t),f(t)⟩}.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(t),f(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(f(t))^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(t+{t}^{2})^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}({t}^{2}+2{t}^{3}+{t}^{4})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{t}^{3}}{3}+\\frac{{t}^{4}}{2}+\\frac{{t}^{5}}{5})|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}+8+\\frac{32}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{256}{15}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n‖f(t)‖=\\sqrt{\\frac{256}{15}}=\\frac{16}{\\sqrt{15}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529137 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133814 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "92053541-63fa-5cca-b3d8-0f4864c31051" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Norm of a Vector With Respect to a Given Inner Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "365ca546-2c5d-5019-a455-b4999bc2be24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{23}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528439} {:answer/id #uuid "8801b776-a19a-596b-b075-b22735277384" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528626} {:answer/id #uuid "b314f0bf-f9e4-5eb6-8317-c15e1e7bc15f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528739} {:answer/id #uuid "cb92e58e-5247-58b6-b945-2ce280bce11f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528798} {:answer/id #uuid "cd7fdef6-0c83-5dab-a365-d572940ee5d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528805}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b314f0bf-f9e4-5eb6-8317-c15e1e7bc15f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528739} :answer-field/id #uuid "c630f8e1-0324-5294-a68b-04d4d6edff9d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186529048}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6e2c74ef-5be6-50fe-9eda-c944716ab881" :question/math-academy-id "q-43906" :question/problem "An inner product on $V={R}^{3}$ is defined as $⟨x,y⟩={x}_{1}{y}_{1}+3{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{y}_{3}.$ \nCalculate the norm of the vector $v=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ under this inner product." :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $v$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖=\\sqrt{⟨v,v⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $‖v‖$ using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖ & =\\sqrt{⟨v,v⟩} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2\\cdot 2+3\\cdot ((-1)\\cdot (-1))+2\\cdot (3\\cdot 3)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+3+18} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329744 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133814 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "92053541-63fa-5cca-b3d8-0f4864c31051" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Norm of a Vector With Respect to a Given Inner Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "395a6f52-7ea0-50c3-af8b-ac5ad3661be1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{37}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327434} {:answer/id #uuid "42441db6-dc19-520d-ad98-5a327b95900d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327516} {:answer/id #uuid "42998bba-dce3-55cf-a5cb-7196b6c3c611" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327517} {:answer/id #uuid "7e030380-492c-55d2-8314-1a4d2812b70a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328022} {:answer/id #uuid "da4542b6-69ff-5629-970e-e1d094047d5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328844}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42998bba-dce3-55cf-a5cb-7196b6c3c611" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327517} :answer-field/id #uuid "dcf24b07-bfc2-5211-9a6e-78c75fd5dbe9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329571}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "44115ef9-3207-523e-bdcf-a1809df46edc" :question/math-academy-id "q-43908" :question/problem "An inner product on $V={R}^{3}$ is defined as $⟨x,y⟩={x}_{1}{y}_{1}+4{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+7{x}_{3}{y}_{3}.$ \nCalculate the norm of the vector $v=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$ under this inner product." :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $v$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖=\\sqrt{⟨v,v⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $‖v‖$ using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖ & =\\sqrt{⟨v,v⟩} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3\\cdot 3+4\\cdot ((-2)\\cdot (-2))+7\\cdot (0\\cdot 0)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364192 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133767 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e023193-7494-5e3a-bd6e-e15ae0e9a1bd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Norm of a Vector in an Inner Product Space of Polynomials"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62cb51ae-cde1-5a2e-abc8-cd20312e842a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "132" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364194} {:answer/id #uuid "4609a3ac-8420-5679-8640-a675f61f59fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{133}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364195} {:answer/id #uuid "1c34c7ef-f88e-530d-a724-79beaa3af61f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{32}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364196} {:answer/id #uuid "f444d193-8f08-5839-b41c-5798b242ab56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "133" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364197} {:answer/id #uuid "9e0f3efe-3665-5e7d-9acd-8bb0e688bba0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{33}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364198}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e0f3efe-3665-5e7d-9acd-8bb0e688bba0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{33}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364198} :answer-field/id #uuid "1dfe3a96-87fa-5c11-81f3-41a4a8eda860" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364193}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "541ce81a-785c-54c8-9270-c091e7c9bd9b" :question/math-academy-id "q-43918" :question/problem "Let $V={R}_{2}[t]$ be the vector space of all polynomials of degree at most $2,$ equipped with the inner product\n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩=x(1)y(1)+x(2)y(2)+x(3)y(3).\n$$\n\nCalculate the norm of the vector $p(t)=10-2{t}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $p(t)$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖p(t)‖=\\sqrt{⟨p(t),p(t)⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $p(t)=10-2{t}^{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\np(1)=8,\\,p(2)=2,\\,p(3)=-8.\n$$\n\nComputing $‖p(t)‖$ using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖p(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{⟨p(t),p(t)⟩} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{p(1)p(1)+p(2)p(2)+p(3)p(3)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{[p(1)]^{2}+[p(2)]^{2}+[p(3)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(8)^{2}+(2)^{2}+(-8)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{64+4+64} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{132} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{33}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329747 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133769 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "466fb505-1ff3-5b27-a5f7-0ea5b31b2927" :knowledge-point/title "Normalizing a Vector in an Inner Product Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "292ee882-fdd8-526d-b70e-40cd3b095055" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}(1-\\sqrt{t})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327285} {:answer/id #uuid "2de0c74e-c444-59b9-9c35-bcb115d72350" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}(1-\\sqrt{t})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327345} {:answer/id #uuid "a56a7648-7f94-514a-b990-8a9c2b9950c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1-\\sqrt{t}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328360} {:answer/id #uuid "b4e6b93b-f118-588b-b09e-eb6bed696aff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}(1-\\sqrt{t})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328507} {:answer/id #uuid "ebd53ae4-8b46-57ae-8461-b5d97450b4e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3(1-\\sqrt{t})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328999}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "292ee882-fdd8-526d-b70e-40cd3b095055" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}(1-\\sqrt{t})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186327285} :answer-field/id #uuid "320abe91-41ca-5c8e-ba83-478ea5a519e6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186329276}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1859f87f-98e7-5154-9cca-0bca8773c332" :question/math-academy-id "q-43926" :question/problem "Let $V=C[0,1]$ be the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[0,1],$ equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{1}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nNormalize the vector $f(t)=1-\\sqrt{t}.$" :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $f(t)$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n‖f(t)‖=\\sqrt{⟨f(t),f(t)⟩}.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(t),f(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{(1-\\sqrt{t})}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,(1-2\\sqrt{t}+t),\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={(t-\\frac{4{t}^{3/2}}{3}+\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2})|}_{0}^{1}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =1-\\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n‖f(t)‖=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}.\n$$\n\nTo normalize the vector $f(t),$ we divide $f(t)$ by its norm $‖f(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t) & =\\frac{f(t)}{‖f(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{(1-\\sqrt{t})}{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}(1-\\sqrt{t})\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329749 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133814 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "92053541-63fa-5cca-b3d8-0f4864c31051" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Norm of a Vector With Respect to a Given Inner Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d2d2039-35e0-52e3-a8dd-1490c2ccf425" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{22}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186328292} {:answer/id #uuid "b09dacf4-bf62-5bd4-9103-e76afce4661b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17