Calculating the Norm of a Vector With Respect to a Given Inner Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0dfce8d9-1d3d-5d8b-87cb-3fb62eba8c47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{22}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357866} {:answer/id #uuid "26bd8280-10fa-5bfc-a251-8f9f30ab1cee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358103} {:answer/id #uuid "4d0631f2-664a-5873-be51-7f89e4fbb794" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358419} {:answer/id #uuid "832ffcc1-d23e-5385-a92d-c118dc074976" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{35}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358905} {:answer/id #uuid "d5d7d29b-9eaf-5299-8ea8-2f1187b9a518" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359625}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "832ffcc1-d23e-5385-a92d-c118dc074976" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{35}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358905} :answer-field/id #uuid "25c3f6a5-e5be-5059-9528-6886f9d6a0be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360054}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "02693454-46b1-5dae-9bee-7d855420592b" :question/math-academy-id "q-97413" :question/problem "An inner product on $V={R}^{3}$ is defined as $⟨x,y⟩=2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+{x}_{3}{y}_{3}.$ \nCalculate the norm of the vector $v=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}$ under this inner product." :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $v$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖=\\sqrt{⟨v,v⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $‖v‖$ using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖ & =\\sqrt{⟨v,v⟩} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2\\cdot (3\\cdot 3)+2\\cdot (2\\cdot 2)+(-3)\\cdot (-3)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{18+8+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{35}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360803 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133767 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e023193-7494-5e3a-bd6e-e15ae0e9a1bd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Norm of a Vector in an Inner Product Space of Polynomials"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0318d52c-d117-5f6f-b545-51710d5eda48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{34}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357786} {:answer/id #uuid "33a6df44-20cd-5b3e-a143-7fa3580cf8b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358210} {:answer/id #uuid "ba210521-38c7-54ee-9be9-cc342423e8e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359367} {:answer/id #uuid "e2294538-990c-5334-9b2c-4fb40fc1d6be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359752} {:answer/id #uuid "ede604ba-8894-5daf-aeda-99a07339a8a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359867}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0318d52c-d117-5f6f-b545-51710d5eda48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{34}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357786} :answer-field/id #uuid "81486b66-999f-5054-a764-c58d4382c938" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360212}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f780565a-c549-514a-8a35-175ab26e2cc8" :question/math-academy-id "q-97422" :question/problem "Let $V={R}_{2}[t]$ be the vector space of all polynomials of degree at most $2,$ equipped with the inner product\n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩=x(1)y(1)+x(0)y(0)+x(-1)y(-1).\n$$\n\nCalculate the norm of the vector $p(t)=4-{t}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $p(t)$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖p(t)‖=\\sqrt{⟨p(t),p(t)⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $p(t)=4-{t}^{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\np(1)=3,\\,p(0)=4,\\,p(-1)=3.\n$$\n\nComputing $‖p(t)‖$ using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖p(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{⟨p(t),p(t)⟩} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{p(1)p(1)+p(0)p(0)+p(-1)p(-1)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{[p(1)]^{2}+[p(0)]^{2}+[p(-1)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(3)^{2}+(4)^{2}+(3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+16+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{34}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186529143 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133767 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e023193-7494-5e3a-bd6e-e15ae0e9a1bd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Norm of a Vector in an Inner Product Space of Polynomials"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "116df7c4-ec26-5aa2-9b40-416a961b75bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528339} {:answer/id #uuid "1fa00b09-aa2e-5df4-ac96-221f4752071a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528384} {:answer/id #uuid "3425195d-9aff-555f-aedc-3c2ff2394fd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528428} {:answer/id #uuid "5a6813eb-8d5c-5891-9a6f-a20bbd0d60b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528511} {:answer/id #uuid "a269ca2f-0828-50e2-9c13-2e3788349d15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{197}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528693}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1fa00b09-aa2e-5df4-ac96-221f4752071a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528384} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a799a47-68c0-5f48-82fe-456dcddb2abb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186528985}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7e56a686-12c8-5112-a821-3890332df74f" :question/math-academy-id "q-97423" :question/problem "Let $V={R}_{2}[t]$ be the vector space of all polynomials of degree at most $2,$ equipped with the inner product\n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩=x(0)y(0)+x(1)y(1)+x(2)y(2).\n$$\n\nCalculate the norm of the vector $p(t)=3t-2{t}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $p(t)$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖p(t)‖=\\sqrt{⟨p(t),p(t)⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $p(t)=3t-2{t}^{2},$ we obtain\n\n$$\np(0)=0,\\,p(1)=1,\\,p(2)=-2.\n$$\n\nComputing $‖p(t)‖$ using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖p(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{⟨p(t),p(t)⟩} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{p(0)p(0)+p(1)p(1)+p(2)p(2)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{[p(0)]^{2}+[p(1)]^{2}+[p(2)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(0)^{2}+(1)^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0+1+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360804 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133767 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5e023193-7494-5e3a-bd6e-e15ae0e9a1bd" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Norm of a Vector in an Inner Product Space of Polynomials"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03cc0d92-cd2d-5320-8616-75a7a696d5cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357792} {:answer/id #uuid "8c282ee6-0d2e-55cc-8114-81895f20aefa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{42}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358968} {:answer/id #uuid "9c5a178a-9f06-50cd-ad5a-c9268878ad8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359118} {:answer/id #uuid "a39ac11e-00d3-56f9-85fd-fd623a91e0c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359176} {:answer/id #uuid "d2c14ff1-92d1-513b-a4f0-faec821d0258" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359594}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c282ee6-0d2e-55cc-8114-81895f20aefa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{42}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358968} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e5fdfd1-65a8-5317-837f-16e518dbe310" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360176}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6510bb7a-b307-5109-b913-722262494bbb" :question/math-academy-id "q-97425" :question/problem "Let $V={R}_{2}[t]$ be the vector space of all polynomials of degree at most $2,$ equipped with the inner product\n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩=x(0)y(0)+x(2)y(2)+x(3)y(3).\n$$\n\nCalculate the norm of the vector $p(t)=5-3t.$" :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $p(t)$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖p(t)‖=\\sqrt{⟨p(t),p(t)⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $p(t)=5-3t,$ we obtain\n\n$$\np(0)=5,\\,p(2)=-1,\\,p(3)=-4.\n$$\n\nComputing $‖p(t)‖$ using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖p(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{⟨p(t),p(t)⟩} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{p(0)p(0)+p(2)p(2)+p(3)p(3)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{[p(0)]^{2}+[p(2)]^{2}+[p(3)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(5)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25+1+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{42}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362237 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133768 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "090d6747-55e2-548b-84f2-88f6c732518f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Norm of a Vector in an Inner Product Space of Continuous Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e362122-a8ce-566d-a4f6-71fc864346b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360890} {:answer/id #uuid "37c411e5-07df-5135-b3cc-c85855e6e77d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3\\pi +5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361090} {:answer/id #uuid "8de03b5f-20dd-5bb9-a61e-6f990c0972f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361467} {:answer/id #uuid "99cbbcf1-82f4-5b24-8dbb-488072874726" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361522} {:answer/id #uuid "da9f9b69-1b29-54e8-99d6-af434d0fed8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{9\\pi +5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361809}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8de03b5f-20dd-5bb9-a61e-6f990c0972f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361467} :answer-field/id #uuid "63460fd7-49d9-512e-9abb-53a4e480241f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362067}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "415714b2-f118-53c1-b9e3-24f1aa607a09" :question/math-academy-id "q-97712" :question/problem "Let $V=C[\\pi ,2\\pi ]$ be the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[\\pi ,2\\pi ],$ equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nCalculate the norm of the vector $f(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+1.$" :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $f(t)$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n‖f(t)‖=\\sqrt{⟨f(t),f(t)⟩}.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(t),f(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }(f(t))^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }\\,(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }\\,(4{cos}^{2}⁡t+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }((2+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi }^{2\\pi }(3+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t+4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(3t+\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t+4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t){|}_{\\pi }^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =(6\\pi +0+0)-(3\\pi +0+0) \\\\  & =3\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we made use of the trigonometric identity \n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡t=\\frac{1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t}{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖f(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{3\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186364634 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133768 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "090d6747-55e2-548b-84f2-88f6c732518f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Norm of a Vector in an Inner Product Space of Continuous Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f65503b-cf8e-52cc-b535-c4e4ac1577d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{\\frac{14}{15}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364636} {:answer/id #uuid "8a3a0ce2-8a79-54fa-8343-e971d2422d99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{\\frac{14}{15}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364637} {:answer/id #uuid "f4455b8e-f267-51f3-aa7d-3fbe77f9d1e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364638} {:answer/id #uuid "2e5bbc39-c4f1-5323-92f9-76aa49514b50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{56}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364639} {:answer/id #uuid "17e0d913-1b89-5074-8bb7-aa0e2c7fe8e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{\\frac{14}{15}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364640}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "17e0d913-1b89-5074-8bb7-aa0e2c7fe8e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{\\frac{14}{15}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364640} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e415229-8430-5c71-8b3d-4d06654a0d86" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364635}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c2ec86a9-5d87-5c18-b457-bd17da5e552f" :question/math-academy-id "q-97713" :question/problem "Let $V=C[-1,1]$ be the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[-1,1],$ equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{-1}^{1}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nCalculate the norm of the vector $f(t)={t}^{2}+1.$" :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $f(t)$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n‖f(t)‖=\\sqrt{⟨f(t),f(t)⟩}.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(t),f(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}(f(t))^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}({t}^{2}+1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}({t}^{4}+2{t}^{2}+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={(\\frac{{t}^{5}}{5}+\\frac{2{t}^{3}}{3}+t)|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{2}{3}+1)-(-\\frac{1}{5}-\\frac{2}{3}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}+\\frac{4}{3}+2 \\\\  & =\\frac{56}{15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n‖f(t)‖=\\sqrt{\\frac{56}{15}}=2\\sqrt{\\frac{14}{15}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362239 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133769 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "466fb505-1ff3-5b27-a5f7-0ea5b31b2927" :knowledge-point/title "Normalizing a Vector in an Inner Product Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34c9ab25-bb44-5b9f-86ff-e85967799d00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{13}(2-3t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361069} {:answer/id #uuid "55332a39-2ade-5b9c-baf3-25a4c2b86f04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{10}(2-3t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361218} {:answer/id #uuid "8436e0bd-b597-5545-bc78-0c3243a99dc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}(2-3t)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361426} {:answer/id #uuid "a9663e2b-84d5-5505-8c70-97de6224b50e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{13}(3t-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361594} {:answer/id #uuid "d3978e98-f734-5377-9be9-002578a2ba06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-3t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361783}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3978e98-f734-5377-9be9-002578a2ba06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-3t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361783} :answer-field/id #uuid "2765081e-d729-5b88-8427-9964ebc29ed1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362016}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "4bb15900-4898-54df-9190-c765e91944f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-97721" :question/problem "Let $V=C[0,1]$ be the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[0,1],$ equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{1}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nNormalize the vector $f(t)=2-3t.$" :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $f(t)$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n‖f(t)‖=\\sqrt{⟨f(t),f(t)⟩}.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(t),f(t)⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{(2-3t)}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\,(4-12t+9{t}^{2})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={(4t-6{t}^{2}+3{t}^{3})|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =4-6+3 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n‖f(t)‖=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo normalize the vector $f(t),$ we divide $f(t)$ by its norm $‖f(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t) & =\\frac{f(t)}{‖f(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{2-3t}{1} \\\\  & =2-3t\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362242 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133769 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "466fb505-1ff3-5b27-a5f7-0ea5b31b2927" :knowledge-point/title "Normalizing a Vector in an Inner Product Space"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "102dd1dc-3f52-5742-81ad-fafc733319ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{22}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360895} {:answer/id #uuid "5de5f5ae-0a79-56e7-9ade-0408aef1c3dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{7}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361261} {:answer/id #uuid "5f22949f-82f7-54f5-8ba5-a1c1968e7fe9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{22}}{22}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361266} {:answer/id #uuid "b0f786ef-ad4b-5ac6-9fcf-664739b71f33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361623} {:answer/id #uuid "f54ed317-3fb7-51eb-bc06-24d95088def1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{35}}{35}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361937}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f54ed317-3fb7-51eb-bc06-24d95088def1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{35}}{35}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361937} :answer-field/id #uuid "b450503f-5356-5052-a295-351b61078c2d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362145}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cc7a4edb-0118-580e-bca0-ed1f0771c326" :question/math-academy-id "q-97726" :question/problem "An inner product on $V={R}^{3}$ is defined as $⟨x,y⟩=2{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+{x}_{3}{y}_{3}.$ \n\nNormalize the  vector $v=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}$ under this inner product." :question/worked-solution "The norm of a vector $v$ with respect to an inner product $⟨\\cdot ,\\cdot ⟩$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖=\\sqrt{⟨v,v⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product using our definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨v,v⟩ & =2\\cdot (3\\cdot 3)+2\\cdot (2\\cdot 2)+(-3)\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =18+8+9 \\\\  & =35.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖v‖ & =\\sqrt{35}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo normalize the vector $v$, we divide $v$ by its norm $‖v‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{v}{‖v‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{35}}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{35}}{35}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
